#: ../../using/watching.rst:2 846082cbdd2742ca9ad9b0c5fecab128
msgid "Watching a drive while it works"
msgstr ""

#: ../../using/watching.rst:4 1ddf0e12362549abb9ff48e10d83de49
msgid ""
"A tape drive is least willing to talk exactly when it is most "
"interesting. For the whole of a backup ``mt`` answers *device busy*, and "
"every tool built on it goes quiet - the program doing the writing has the"
" drive's tape device open, and the kernel gives that to one writer at a "
"time."
msgstr ""

#: ../../using/watching.rst:9 cd533ed450274b7f8ffacd983d1ce480
msgid "Only that one door is shut. This console shows the drive working anyway."
msgstr ""

#: ../../using/watching.rst:16 28a3f13cfa8c4f4aa84ffcc553249fc6
msgid "On the library page"
msgstr ""

#: ../../using/watching.rst:18 1c7c5cf82784419a98673bf319cccbe0
msgid ""
"The **Tape Drives** card has a line per drive, refreshed every five "
"seconds:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../using/watching.rst:20 e8e053ea2db640139677f211915d6eb2
#, python-format
msgid ""
"Drive 31 writing G03001TA, 378.1 MB written, 75.8% of the tape, the\n"
"bar amber; drives 32, 33 and 34 empty"
msgstr ""

#: ../../using/watching.rst:25 dd33095c8ca643feb9322256ebd3047e
msgid ""
"That is library 30 while a drive is actually writing. The bar is how full"
" the cartridge is; it turns amber past 75% and red past 90%, which is why"
" the one above is amber."
msgstr ""

#: ../../using/watching.rst:29 88dcb402d9984549bab79a74ccbc146a
msgid ""
"An empty drive says ``empty``, a drive with a cartridge in it but nothing"
" happening says ``holding``, and the counters keep the last figures until"
" the tape is unloaded - so a finished backup still shows how much it "
"wrote."
msgstr ""

#: ../../using/watching.rst:33 55478a4ef3684eeb800471e3fe742685
msgid "The same panel is on the monitor page, at ``/libraries/monitor/<id>/``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../using/watching.rst:35 18b4929f99d949f2a22c1984c7d8785b
msgid "The monitor page, with what the drives are doing"
msgstr ""

#: ../../using/watching.rst:40 3350cfc9d06846329df1e794c77ccf4f
msgid "On the command line"
msgstr ""

#: ../../using/watching.rst:55 1cbdc18522a54757b87e52df50d354af
msgid ""
"The same sentence the page shows, because both ask one service. Nothing "
"is worked out in the browser."
msgstr ""

#: ../../using/watching.rst:59 315b27305f734fdca44d5a114c382c83
msgid "What the states mean"
msgstr ""

#: ../../using/watching.rst:61 4209aaf871bd4e51957a82ffdd58cb51
msgid "``writing`` / ``reading``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../using/watching.rst:62 45b378380a9044fcb03f0daa52f7a9ca
msgid "The counters grew since the previous reading."
msgstr ""

#: ../../using/watching.rst:64 bae79d75e493443b8844c50241612441
msgid "``holding``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../using/watching.rst:65 82031e7c714d4039a8e828713bf82247
msgid "A cartridge is loaded and the counters did not move."
msgstr ""

#: ../../using/watching.rst:67 8f407a2b66a14a988a638f3a7a073627
msgid "``empty``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../using/watching.rst:68 2ea5e2dec89c4aac9a15bf75faabdf82
msgid "No cartridge in the drive."
msgstr ""

#: ../../using/watching.rst:70 9f1c65743b1749da942b8e4fbbeb4f49
msgid "``silent``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../using/watching.rst:71 3d91c42e3ad94f6b875ce2f8b694b467
msgid ""
"Nothing answered - usually a drive that is stopped. Check with "
"``systemctl status vtltape@31``. It also appears when this console is "
"older than the MHVTL underneath it; upgrading the console settles that."
msgstr ""

#: ../../using/watching.rst:76 6fd0f76fa99f4f1d80efde3175777bc6
msgid "Where the numbers come from"
msgstr ""

#: ../../using/watching.rst:78 97b365e07ae8469e8f71506da95550ff
msgid ""
"The drive keeps its own counters, and the console reads them through a "
"different device file from the one the backup is holding - so the backup "
"never has to be interrupted to see how it is getting on. The robot is "
"asked separately which cartridge is in which drive, because it is the "
"authority on that."
msgstr ""

#: ../../using/watching.rst:84 f5dac4ef9c294cb093e1eb06b217801e
msgid "``written``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../using/watching.rst:85 e95da13e6e5a4fc5845884da8e809c22
msgid "Bytes the backup handed the drive."
msgstr ""

#: ../../using/watching.rst:87 1e34523b3e13440497b070b7cc1366bd
#, python-format
msgid "``% of the tape``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../using/watching.rst:88 abf5c0b18df741429ae8442028b98d7c
msgid ""
"How much of the cartridge is used - measured in what actually went to the"
" medium, which is less than *written* when the data compresses."
msgstr ""

#: ../../using/watching.rst:91 a4dcbd364e4f4709b1b8331c0773af21
msgid "``compression``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../using/watching.rst:92 3c8246a683644929a37cbaa38c75e865
msgid ""
"Bytes in over bytes on the medium. Ordinary files compress about two to "
"one; a ratio of 1.0 is not shown, because most test data does not "
"compress and a clause saying so on every line is noise."
msgstr ""

#: ../../using/watching.rst:97 0686053803534dbdb52ed30e486084db
msgid "Two readings, not one"
msgstr ""

#: ../../using/watching.rst:99 44564b5c3470461eab19d7299463041a
msgid ""
"MHVTL reports totals, not a rate, so *writing* means the number grew "
"since the last reading. A command run once has nothing to compare with "
"and waits a second to read again:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../using/watching.rst:108 1f0b8a7d212d46ed8f92eab138c3aa32
msgid ""
"The web page uses the second form, because it polls: the next refresh is "
"a better answer than a request that blocks."
msgstr ""

#: ../../using/watching.rst:112 1809b9fb858046e4aafa5d44341f4b2d
msgid "If it says ``holding`` while a backup is running"
msgstr ""

#: ../../using/watching.rst:114 64cb5b9cce774b7bbb696c7b581b8d88
msgid ""
"The backup may be writing to a **different drive**. ``mhvtl status "
"library 30`` says which drive holds which cartridge."
msgstr ""

#: ../../using/watching.rst:116 abbd9b67fa6c4bc0879f1fe04da5cb7e
msgid ""
"The two readings may have been more than two minutes apart, which makes "
"the older one useless. Ask again."
msgstr ""

#: ../../using/watching.rst:120 6421f833bd384166826700c3636da359
msgid "If ``mt`` and the panel disagree"
msgstr ""

#: ../../using/watching.rst:122 3d05ffdc161d4b5b83c445c7bdeb8239
msgid ""
"They can, and the panel is usually right. ``mt`` reports what the "
"kernel's tape driver believes, which can be stale:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../using/watching.rst:136 409bd87213414a8ba9512091b7ebbc22
msgid ""
"Two of the three agree that the cartridge is in the drive, and they are "
"the two that matter: the robot moved it there and the daemon holds it. "
"See :doc:`../running/when-something-is-wrong`."
msgstr ""

